[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Sicilian Defense: Alapin Variation"]
[Variation "Alapin Variation, Barmen Defense"]
[ECO "B22"]
[Character "tactical"]
[Risk "medium"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "trap,pawn-grab"]
[Themes "tempo-gain,loose-pawn"]
[For "white"]
[Kind "against-us"]
[Opponent "3...Qxd5"]
[Start "1. e4 c5 2. c3 d5 3. exd5 Qxd5 4. d4 Nf6"]

5. c4 $2 { Looks like a free tempo on the queen, but the c3 pawn was the one guarding d4. Once it leaves, the pawn on d4 is attacked twice and defended only by the queen. } 5... Qxd4 { Takes a pawn and attacks the rook on a1 and the pawn on c4 as well. } 6. Qb3 { Dodges the queen trade, but Black has won a clean pawn and White has nothing to show for it. } 6... Nc6 7. Nf3 Qd6 *
